```cpp
otError Mle::AppendNetworkData(Message &aMessage, bool aStableOnly)
{
    otError        error = OT_ERROR_NONE;
    NetworkDataTlv tlv;

    VerifyOrExit(!mRetrieveNewNetworkData, error = OT_ERROR_INVALID_STATE);

    tlv.Init();
    FillNetworkDataTlv(tlv, aStableOnly);

    error = aMessage.AppendTlv(tlv);

exit:
    return error;
}
```

`AppendTlv` is:
```cpp
otError Message::AppendTlv(const Tlv &aTlv)
{
    return Append(&aTlv, aTlv.GetSize());
}
```

`GetSize()` returns `sizeof(Tlv) + GetLength()`. If `GetLength()` is set to some value by `FillNetworkDataTlv`, then `GetSize()` returns `2 + length`, and `Append` tries to read `2 + length` bytes from `&tlv`, but `tlv` is only 2 bytes on the stack!

But `FillNetworkDataTlv` sets `length = 0` initially, and `GetNetworkData` only modifies `length` if `mLength == 0` (in which case it stays 0). So `GetLength()` should be 0.

